## Working principles

The working principles (reproduce-on-latest-Kit first, defaults-first, no invented numbers, no customer attribution, doc links inline, mark experimental/deprecated) are maintained once in [AGENTS.md](mdc:AGENTS.md) — read them there so they can't drift between files. Editing or building the guide itself? See [AUTHORING.md](mdc:AUTHORING.md) for the Sphinx conventions, build, and git workflow.

## Behavior expectations

- Quote specific setting paths verbatim (e.g. `/app/usdrt/population/utils/mergeMaterials`, never just `mergeMaterials`).
- Flag when guidance depends on Kit version. Most defaults assume Kit 109 / 110.
- Don't fabricate code samples — the runnable examples in `skills/usdrt-advisor/SKILL.md` and `docs/reference/usd-in-kit.md` are intentionally complete (with imports). Copy from those rather than inventing variants.

## When the question doesn't match any skill

If the user's question doesn't fit one of the skills in AGENTS.md, answer directly using the canonical chapter in `docs/` rather than guessing. The chapter mapping is documented in [AGENTS.md](mdc:AGENTS.md) under "Document layout".
